+## Proposed — awaiting Justin Philpott
+
+These are proposals from the 2026-10-07 entropy assessment, not decisions. Each becomes a dated, attributed entry
+below once decided, or is deleted if rejected. Work that depends on one waits for it.
+
+### P1 (proposed): INTENT.md changes only on the steward's recorded decision
+
+**Context**: No file names who decides what this project is for. `AGENTS.md` ("Consult INTENT.md for significant
+decisions") and `INTENT.md`'s header tell any contributor, including an agent, to update `INTENT.md` directly with a
+dated note, but `INTENT.md` keeps a single "Last revised" line, so the reasons for earlier revisions are already
+gone. Justin Philpott's recorded choices on scope (`explorations/2026-03-24-entropy-immune-system-conversation.md`)
+show him acting as the decider.
+**Proposal**: Name Justin Philpott as steward in `AGENTS.md` and the `INTENT.md` header. Contributors record a
+proposed intent change here, under this heading; `INTENT.md` changes after his recorded decision. A correction that
+an existing decision already settles may be made directly, citing it.
+**Alternative**: Record a standing delegation: contributors may revise `INTENT.md` directly, keeping a dated
+revision log at its foot.
+**Depends on it**: `AGENTS.md` "Consult INTENT.md…" wording; the Intent section of `skills/local/entropy-guard`.
+
+### P2 (proposed): session-coherence-skill-generator is the only skill that writes guards
+
+**Context**: Two skills write guards. `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 generates or refines them, and
+`README.md` "How to use this repo" routes guard generation there; `session-coherence-skill-generator` also generates
+them, and has the young-repo bootstrap mode (entry below). `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle" names only the
+assessment workflow as generator. `guards-integrator` says `entropy-assessment` generates guards, which it no longer
+does. No entry records adding the generator or how it relates to the assessments.
+**Proposal**: The assessments analyse and hand their findings and checks to `session-coherence-skill-generator`,
+which alone builds or amends guards; `guards-integrator` takes its output. The front door routes young repos to the
+generator's bootstrap mode. This follows "Guard creation skills over guard libraries" (one creation skill) and
+"Consolidate domain generators…" (which removed duplicated generator scaffolding).
+**Alternatives**: Keep guard writing in the assessments and narrow the generator to generic session-handoff guards
+and bootstrap; or fold bootstrap mode into the assessments and retire the generator.
+**Depends on it**: `INTENT.md` "The guard lifecycle"; `README.md` "How to use this repo"; `docs-first-planning-
+assessment` Phase 2; `entropy-assessment` Step 3; `guards-integrator` "When to Run" and "What This Is Not".
+
+### P3 (proposed): the validation batch records session outcomes first, and merges where a PR flow exists
+
+**Context**: "Farm broader entropic-immunity exploration…" below sets the next loop as open source projects measured
+by merged PRs. `INTENT.md` (revised 2026-04-07), `README.md` "Project status" and `TODO.md` "Next Up" set it as
+docs-first planning repos measured by clearer session recovery, fewer reintroduced stale ideas and more coherent
+docs. "Specialize first…" narrowed the target set but said nothing about the measure. Justin Philpott's first
+evidence of value was fixes merged within minutes (`explorations/2026-03-19-autopoiesis.md`, opening).
+**Proposal**: For each target, record the `INTENT.md` outcomes, and also whether the resulting changes merged when
+the target has a PR flow. Mark the "Farm…" entry partially superseded on the target set and measure.
+**Alternatives**: Merged PRs only; session outcomes only.
+**Depends on it**: `TODO.md` "Next Up" item 2; how batch results are recorded.
+
